@jason810496 @potiuk, I have few questions from the community before making a proposal,
1. How strongly do we want the Breeze CLI to remain the single source of truth for agent skills? Should the skills be entirely generated from CLI metadata, or should there be an intermediate schema describing workflows that Breeze commands map into?
2. If Breeze CLI evolves, do maintainers expect the AI skill layer to adapt automatically through the prek sync mechanism, or should we maintain some backward compatibility layer for agents?

@Abhishekmishra2808  Yes, that matches my understanding so far as well.

The agent skill layer’s source of truth would be the contributing documentation, modelling the workflow of how a real contributor interacts with the development environment.

and yes, breeze metadata can still be useful at the execution layer to derive or validate how those workflows map to Breeze commands when needed.

@jason810496 @potiuk — updated the POC based on the source of truth discussion.
Added `.. agent-skill::` blocks directly inside `contributing-docs/03_contributors_quick_start.rst` so the skills live where contributors already read about the workflows. The extractor now picks them up from there instead of a separate file.
PR: https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/63661
